 "Spend your energy on purpose", "Your baseline and symptoms shape the plan.", ["Daily plans within your energy envelope", "Boom-bust pattern detection", "Crash plans and scripts for others"],
 [NAME, CH("condition", "Condition", ["ME/CFS", "Fibromyalgia", "Long COVID", "POTS", "Other / undiagnosed"]), NUM("spoons", "Spoons on a typical day", "10"), CH("pem", "Post-exertional crashes", ["Rarely", "Sometimes", "Most weeks", "Constant"])],
 [T("day", "Plan today", "Fit tasks to your spoons", "🥄", [LONG("tasks", "What needs doing", "shower, GP call, cook dinner, reply to 5 emails, kids' pickup"), CH("today", "Energy right now vs usual", ["Lower", "About usual", "Higher"], "About usual")],
    "Budget today for the profile spoons with energy '{today}' across: {tasks}. Table (Task | Spoon cost | Do, delegate, defer or drop | Time slot | Rest after), a checklist of the plan in order with rest blocks as their own items, bullets on cutting each task's cost (sit down, batch, timers, pre-prepared food), and a callout to keep 2 spoons in reserve and what a crash warning typically feels like for this condition.", "table, checklist, bullets, callout", "Budget it", "Counting spoons…"),
  T("pattern", "Boom-bust check", "Paste a couple of weeks", "📉", [LONG("log", "Activity and symptom log", "Mon: big clean, felt great; Tue–Thu: crashed, couldn't work; Fri: pushed to do the shopping…")],
    "Analyse: {log}. Table (Day | Activity level 1–5 | Symptoms 1–5 | Pattern note), bullets identifying boom-bust cycles, the typical crash delay in hours or days and the activity threshold that seems to trigger it, a kv with a suggested sustainable daily baseline and a rule for when to increase it, and a callout that the first goal of pacing is to stabilise and that increases are only for weeks that have been stable.", "table, bullets, kv, callout", "Find cycles", "Spotting the bust…"),
  T("crash", "Crash plan", "Get through the next 72 hours", "🛏️", [CH("severity", "How bad", ["Mild", "Moderate", "Severe, bed-bound"], "Moderate"), TXT("obligations", "What can't wait", "kids' dinner, one work message")],
    "A 72-hour crash plan at '{severity}' with obligations '{obligations}'. Steps for each day (rest positions, low-stimulation environment, hydration and easy food, minimum-effort ways to meet the obligations), a checklist of what to ask a partner, friend or delivery service to do, a quote with a 2-line message to send someone who can help, and a callout on symptoms that are not typical of a crash (chest pain, new weakness, severe breathlessness) and need medical care.", "steps, checklist, quote, callout", "Plan the crash", "Dimming everything…"),
  T("explain", "Explain my limits", "Scripts for work, family, friends", "💬", [CH("who", "To", ["Manager", "Partner", "Parent", "Friend who doesn't get it", "Doctor"], "Friend who doesn't get it"), TXT("situation", "The situation", "they keep inviting me to late dinners and get hurt when I cancel")],
    "Write for my {who} about: {situation}. A quote with a short, warm, boundary-clear message, bullets of 3 alternative ways to keep the relationship or job working (shorter, earlier, remote, split tasks), a kv of one-line answers to common pushbacks ('but you look fine', 'just try exercising'), and a callout on not over-explaining or apologising.", "quote, bullets, kv, callout", "Write it", "Finding words…"),
  T("gentle", "Gentle movement check", "Only if you're stable", "🌿", [CH("weeks", "Weeks since last crash", ["Under 2", "2–4", "Over 4"], "2–4"), CH("now", "Currently manage", ["Bed to chair", "Short walks indoors", "Walks under 10 min", "Walks 10–30 min"], "Short walks indoors")],
    "Weeks since the last crash: {weeks}. Currently manages: '{now}'. Decide whether any increase is appropriate for the profile. Text with a clear yes or not-yet verdict and why, a table (Week | Activity | Minutes | Stop rule) for 4 weeks that increases by no more than 10% and only after symptom-stable weeks, bullets on heart-rate pacing and recumbent options for POTS, and a callout that graded exercise therapy is not recommended for ME/CFS with post-exertional malaise and that any plan stops at the first sign of PEM.", "text, table, bullets, callout", "Check", "Weighing gently…")],
